Notebook[{
Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Trilinear Basis Functions\n",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 "\"xc\" variables are in the canonical cube element. Derivatives in \"x\" \
are computed via the chain rule. Since we only allow axis-aligned stretches \
of the canonical cube, these chain rules only involve dividing by width, \
height, and depth."
}], "Text",
